From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Kerr <charles@charleskerr.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:39:59 -0600
Subject: test: accept GMT+00:00 as Europe/Dublin's winter time zone name

Chromium's ICU moved to tzdb 2026f, whose metazone data maps
Europe/Dublin only to the Irish metazone from 1971 on. English has no
standard-time name for that metazone, so in winter the long time zone
name falls back to "GMT+00:00" instead of "Greenwich Mean Time". The
test still checks that the TZ change takes effect: the previous zone
(America/Los_Angeles) and UTC never format this way.

tzdb 2026c had the same mapping and 2026e restored the GMT one. Remove
this patch once Chromium's ICU maps Europe/Dublin to GMT again.

Refs: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/deps/icu/+/8701116
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/test/parallel/test-datetime-change-notify.js b/test/parallel/test-datetime-change-notify.js
index 01843511907077857be22c9bc7e7f8568fc677d1..65aa1b08907f76e921afaad78ac1e5a59a86379f 100644
--- a/test/parallel/test-datetime-change-notify.js
+++ b/test/parallel/test-datetime-change-notify.js
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ const cases = [
   },
   {
     timeZone: 'Europe/Dublin',
-    expected: /Irish Standard Time|Greenwich Mean Time/,
+    // Chromium's ICU (tzdb 2026f) has no English winter name for Dublin.
+    expected: /Irish Standard Time|Greenwich Mean Time|GMT\+00:00/,
   },
 ];
 
